@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Concurrent motion · independent jobs and persistent ICC buffers
caption Motor-disconnected application fixture; physical commissioning remains separate.
footer Heartbeat 100 ms / deadline 500 ms and ownership lease 250 ms are unchanged.
autonumber
actor CLI
box "M7 · UI" #EDF4FE
participant "Client / Planner" as C
participant "ICC sender" as U
end box
boundary "Shared-memory transport" as T #FFF5DF
box "M4 · IO" #EAF7F4
participant "ICC sender / receiver" as S
participant "Server / Controller" as E
participant "Executor / timer DMA" as D
end box
note over U,S
  Each lane's long-lived send coroutine owns one frame buffer.
  A synchronous helper fills it; transport borrows its span.
  Reuse waits for send completion. No full-frame coroutine
  is allocated for each message or heartbeat.
  M4 ordinary dispatch/admission executes from SDRAM.
  STEP/IRQ and bounded transport hot paths remain in internal SRAM.
end note
CLI -> C : axis jog shoulder -.2 --continuous
C -> U : acquire, prepare, run
U -> T : serialized request
T -> S : deliver
S -> E : admit Axis-family job
E -> D : rolling shoulder program + installed brake
E --> C : Running (through ICC)
CLI -> C : axis move elbow -1
C -> S : independent-axis acquire / prepare / run (via ICC)
S -> E : validate reservation and revisions
E -> D : elbow program; shoulder continues
loop while motion is active
  U -> S : urgent heartbeat (via transport)
  S --> U : acknowledgement using persistent sender buffer
  C -> E : ownership renewal (via urgent service)
  E -> D : local schedule maintenance
end
D --> E : elbow completed; exact pulse count
E --> C : terminal result; release elbow ownership
CLI -> C : axis stop shoulder
C -> E : urgent controlled stop (via ICC)
E -> D : select installed stopping continuation
D --> E : shoulder stopped
E --> C : terminal result; release shoulder ownership
note over CLI,D #EAF7F4
  Repeated overlap / stop / restart and analyzer checks pass.
  The new host test forbids full-frame allocations during
  heartbeat traffic after startup. This is not a maximum-rate
  or powered-mechanics qualification.
end note
@enduml
